# Rank 1528 / CVE-2023-27596: OpenSIPS' codec-stripping functions
# trimmed trailing spaces by walking a pointer backwards with no
# lower bound, so a crafted codec parameter walked off the start of
# the parsed value and read whatever preceded it (out-of-bounds read,
# CWE-125; GHSA-3ghx-j39m-cw4f, found in the 2021/2022 security
# audit by Enable Security). The loops in modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c
# did `while (*(--tmp) == ' ') { ... }` -- tmp starts somewhere
# inside lmp->u.value and the pre-decrement runs unchecked even when
# the whole value is spaces or empty, stepping before the buffer and
# dereferencing. Pool commit dd051f8ed5 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK --
# "[sipmsgops] fix codec_delete_XX() parsing", one line): the walk is
# bounded with `while (tmp > lmp->u.value && *(--tmp) == ' ')`. No
# pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, reverse-walk bounds. The defect is a pointer loop whose
# only exit is the pointed-to byte -- no relation between the cursor
# and the buffer it started from -- the same parser-walk family as
# ranks 1527 (cursor-role separation) and 1559 (wire budget): the
# corpus's memory rules label derefs and frees, not walk-bound
# discipline, and asking "does every backwards step stay above the
# buffer start" is loop-carried bound vocabulary. A binding on
# OpenSIPS' own codecs.c would detect this module rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning codecs.c reports the
# same 20 findings at both revisions (1 at high; none change with the
# bound). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped.
# Spec cve_rank1528 records the unbounded backward trim and the
# bounded form -- the two snippets differ only in the tmp >
# lmp->u.value guard -- both asserting reject VYQL-MEM-006: when
# walk-bound vocabulary lands, the unbounded form must flip to
# expect.

test "rank1528: the space trim walks back without a floor"
  lang c
  file modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  code
  ```
  struct lump {
      union {
          char value[64];
      } u;
  };

  int trim_codec(struct lump *lmp, int codec_len)
  {
      char *tmp = lmp->u.value + codec_len;

      while (*(--tmp) == ' ') {
          codec_len--;
      }

      return codec_len;
  }
  ```

test "rank1528: the fix bounds the walk to the value start"
  lang c
  file modules/sipmsgops/codecs.c
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  code
  ```
  struct lump {
      union {
          char value[64];
      } u;
  };

  int trim_codec(struct lump *lmp, int codec_len)
  {
      char *tmp = lmp->u.value + codec_len;

      while (tmp > lmp->u.value && *(--tmp) == ' ') {
          codec_len--;
      }

      return codec_len;
  }
  ```
